{"id":"72e182f3-6125-4e92-a06e-135db6d99a4e","companyId":"8ee81b47-0030-4cee-ac57-0fb6f0ae78d7","conversationAgentId":null,"conversationUserId":null,"conversationState":null,"conversationSessionGeneration":0,"conversationBoundaryCommentId":null,"projectId":"0de691a5-09fe-4779-9ab5-2792af15e4b1","projectWorkspaceId":null,"goalId":null,"parentId":"114aee21-4ade-4ddd-93e8-de555ce90f01","title":"Establish the MOSAIC knowledge base","description":"Establish SHERIDAN+BAIRNS' authoritative MOSAIC knowledge baseline under the [approved plan](/SHE/issues/SHE-1#document-plan).\n\nOwner: The Oracle. Can start now: hire is active and source inventory can begin with https://groundstoact.com/ and accessible company materials. This is a separate task because it belongs to the MOSAIC curator and supplies a hard knowledge dependency for the website work.\n\nDeliver documents on this task:\n- Source register with URLs or file references, dates, versions and provenance.\n- Versioned core reference separating established MOSAIC principles, supporting evidence, inference, proposed extensions and unresolved founder-intent questions.\n- Plain-language glossary, worked example, FAQ and open-question log.\n- An explicit inventory of missing source access; do not invent missing framework details.\n\nPreserve the founder's framework; do not silently redefine it. Request genuinely necessary missing material through a saved question card and in_review. Use existing public sources first. Present the baseline for founder review through a real interaction before treating disputed content as authoritative. Chief of Staff owns coordination and the downstream website draft; provide source-linked accuracy guidance when requested.\n\nAcceptance: all listed artifacts are inspectable on this task, substantive claims trace to sources, conflicts and uncertainty are labeled, and founder review has resolved or explicitly bounded material uncertainty. No publication, participant recruitment, extra hires or unapproved tasks.\n\nContext: the company turns fragmented, messy data and evidence into defensible, consequential decisions. Monetisation remains open across software, consulting and services. The eventual website target is at least 8 of the same 10 people both explaining what MOSAIC is/how it works and scoring at least 4/5 on a quiz; this task provides the foundation, not evidence that the target has been met.","status":"done","statusVersion":6,"lastStatusDecisionId":null,"workMode":"standard","harnessKind":null,"priority":"medium","reviewPolicy":null,"assigneeAgentId":"53401070-9c11-47c2-9a1f-ba4b54d7da3d","assigneeUserId":null,"checkoutRunId":null,"executionRunId":null,"executionAgentNameKey":null,"executionLockedAt":null,"createdByAgentId":"fdf9690b-d2b7-438d-a0cf-59f0cfd245f2","createdByUserId":null,"responsibleUserId":"local-board","issueNumber":2,"identifier":"SHE-2","originKind":"manual","originId":null,"originRunId":"154f1a8c-2c78-4c84-a06d-b4b7ea1f252d","originIdentityContextId":"6a5f533c-a25e-4a80-b7af-3dab2315bab6","continuationIdentityContextId":"622d05d7-d2cc-47b3-b6bf-2bf00d7a0793","originFingerprint":"default","requestDepth":0,"billingCode":null,"assigneeAdapterOverrides":null,"executionPolicy":null,"executionState":null,"monitorNextCheckAt":null,"monitorWakeRequestedAt":null,"monitorLastTriggeredAt":null,"monitorAttemptCount":0,"monitorNotes":null,"monitorScheduledBy":null,"executionWorkspaceId":null,"executionWorkspacePreference":null,"executionWorkspaceSettings":null,"sourceTrust":null,"unblockDescriptor":null,"blockedTransitionAt":null,"blockedOwnerNotifiedAt":null,"startedAt":"2026-09-27T20:22:46.045Z","completedAt":"2026-09-27T20:24:52.490Z","cancelledAt":null,"hiddenAt":null,"createdAt":"2026-09-27T19:39:23.652Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-27T20:25:49.182Z","labels":[],"labelIds":[],"watchdog":null,"ancestors":[{"id":"114aee21-4ade-4ddd-93e8-de555ce90f01","identifier":"SHE-1","title":"Paperclip onboarding","description":"This is the user's first task in Paperclip. Your job is to understand what they want and propose a path forward. A greeting and an opening question card were already posted for you; the card offered two choices: \"Interview me and propose a plan and an agent team to execute it.\" (option `interview`) or \"I have a task in mind\" (option `task`, with a text field). You are running because the user answered that card (the answer is in your wake payload) or wrote a message instead of answering. Don't re-introduce yourself and don't post the opening card again.\n\nWork in this order.\n\n1. Take the path the user picked.\n\n   - `interview` → reply with ONE ask_user_questions card of 3–4 questions that pin down what the organization does, what they want to achieve first, any constraints (time, budget, tools), and what \"done\" looks like. Don't guess; ask. Don't post anything else before the card. The answers lead to the plan-and-team path in step 2.\n\n   - `task` → the text they typed is the task. If it is clear enough to propose on, go straight to step 2. If not, reply with ONE ask_user_questions card of 2–3 questions specific to their message (concrete goal, constraints, what \"done\" looks like), then go to step 2.\n\n   - If they wrote a message instead of answering the card, treat the message as the `task` path.\n\n2. Propose, don't decide. From what you now know, pick the path:\n\n   - They want a plan and/or a team → write a short `plan` document (goal, approach, team as one line per hire: name, role, responsibility; follow-up tasks). Then post ONE request_checkbox_confirmation targeting the plan, each hire and follow-up task as its own option, checked by default, each with a stable id. Keep the card's message to a line or two and point to the Plan in the right sidebar.\n\n   - They want one thing done now → post ONE request_confirmation that says, in a few lines, what you will do and what they will get (and by when, if you can say). No plan document.\n\n3. Wait. Do nothing until a card is accepted. If they ask for changes, revise and re-confirm. Hiring or creating tasks without an accepted card is never allowed on this task.\n\n4. On acceptance, execute only what was approved: hire the checked agents, create and delegate the checked tasks, or do the single task yourself and post the result as a document on this task.","status":"done","priority":"medium","assigneeAgentId":"fdf9690b-d2b7-438d-a0cf-59f0cfd245f2","projectId":"0de691a5-09fe-4779-9ab5-2792af15e4b1","goalId":null,"project":{"id":"0de691a5-09fe-4779-9ab5-2792af15e4b1","name":"Onboarding","description":null,"status":"in_progress","goalId":null,"workspaces":[],"primaryWorkspace":null},"goal":null}],"blockerAttention":{"state":"none","reason":null,"unresolvedBlockerCount":0,"coveredBlockerCount":0,"stalledBlockerCount":0,"attentionBlockerCount":0,"pendingFinalizeBlockerIssueIds":[],"sampleBlockerIdentifier":null,"sampleStalledBlockerIdentifier":null,"blockingTreeLive":false,"directBlockerIssueId":null,"terminalBlockerIssueId":null,"terminalBlocker":null},"reviewAttention":{"state":"none","paths":[],"reason":null},"successfulRunHandoff":null,"executionBlocker":null,"scheduledRetry":null,"activeRecoveryAction":null,"blockedBy":[],"blocks":[{"id":"0a5dea00-395c-4a4e-9230-ce8617bca695","identifier":"SHE-3","title":"Prepare a clearer MOSAIC website and comprehension test","status":"in_progress","priority":"medium","assigneeAgentId":"fdf9690b-d2b7-438d-a0cf-59f0cfd245f2","assigneeUserId":null,"scheduledRetry":null,"activeRecoveryAction":null}],"relatedWork":{"outbound":[{"issue":{"id":"0a5dea00-395c-4a4e-9230-ce8617bca695","identifier":"SHE-3","title":"Prepare a clearer MOSAIC website and comprehension test","status":"in_progress","priority":"medium","assigneeAgentId":"fdf9690b-d2b7-438d-a0cf-59f0cfd245f2","assigneeUserId":null},"mentionCount":5,"sources":[{"kind":"comment","sourceRecordId":"310ac004-d3c9-4a24-9ba3-a175b5f17dd9","label":"comment","matchedText":"/SHE/issues/SHE-3"},{"kind":"comment","